 "stale": false,
 "narrative": "Hay supplies remain tight, with prices continuing to increase steadily in some areas. Producers are facing increased harvest pressure as they work to complete field activities ahead of the first freeze. Some feedlots are adjusting rations by incorporating failed corn and milo to reduce alfalfa usage amid elevated prices. Demand for alfalfa pellets remains strong, while supplies continue to be limited. According to the US Drought Monitor for the week of November 5th, in the High Plains, widespread precipitation resulted in 1-category improvements to the western third Colorado along with parts of the Northern to Central Great Plains. Recent precipitation and the \"convergence of evidence\" supported discontinuing the D3 in most of the Nebraska Panhandle. In Kansas, the categorical percent area of abnormally dry conditions (D0) decreased to 23%, Moderate drought (D1) decreased to 11%, severe drought (D2) decreased to 2%, and there was no extreme drought (D3) or exceptional drought (D4) recorded with 64% of the state experiencing no drought. Prices below reflect the average price. There could be prices higher and lower prices than those published. \nRFV Chart\nAlfalfa Quality Guidelines  \nQuality       ADF           NDF        *RFV/RFQ       **TDN-100%      **TDN-90%        CP \nSupreme     <27          <34         >185                  >62                       >55.9              >22 \nPremium     27-29     34-36       170-185           60.5-62                54.5-55.9        20-22 \nGood            29-32     36-40       150-170           58-60                   52.5-54.5        18-20 \nFair               32-35    40-44        130-150           56-58                   50.5-52.5        16-18 \nUtility            >35         >44            <130               <56                        <50.5              <16  \n*RFV calculated using the Wis/Minn formula. **TDN calculated using the Western formula. Quantitative factors are approximate, and many factors can affect feeding value. Values based on 100% dry matter (TDN showing both 100% & 90%). Guidelines are to be used with visual appearance and intent of sale (usage).",
